e and Cyprian.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":144,"t":"Chapter 22.-The Necessity of Variety in Style.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":145,"t":"Chapter 23.-How the Various Styles Should Be Mingled.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":146,"t":"Chapter 24.-The Effects Produced by the Majestic Style.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":147,"t":"Chapter 25.-How the Temperate Style is to Be Used.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":148,"t":"Chapter 26.-In Every Style the Orator Should Aim at Perspicuity, Beauty, and Persuasiveness.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":149,"t":"Chapter 27.-The Man Whose Life is in Harmony with His Teaching Will Teach with Greater Effect.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":150,"t":"Chapter 28.-Truth is More Important Than Expression.what is Meant by Strifeabout Words.","c":2,"path":["Book 4"],"url":"https://github.com/HistoricalChristianFaith/Writings-Database/tree/master/Augustine%20of%20Hippo/On%20Christian%20Doctrine"},{"n":151,"t":"Chapter 29.-It is Permissible for a Preacher to Deliver to the People What Has Been Written by a More Eloquent Man Than Himself.","c"